# Generated by Cargo
# will have compiled files and executables
debug
target

# These are backup files generated by rustfmt
**/*.rs.bk

# MSVC Windows builds of rustc generate these, which store debugging information
*.pdb

# Generated by cargo mutants
# Contains mutation testing data
**/mutants.out*/

# RustRover
#  JetBrains specific template is maintained in a separate JetBrains.gitignore that can
#  be found at https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Global/JetBrains.gitignore
#  and can be added to the global gitignore or merged into this file.  For a more nuclear
#  option (not recommended) you can uncomment the following to ignore the entire idea folder.
#.idea/

.DS_Store
*.log
node_modules/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.codex/*
!.codex/config.toml
.devin/*
!.devin/config.json
.worktrees
.claude/settings.local.json
.mcp.local.json
.claude/soleur-welcomed.local
.claude/ralph-loop.*.local.md
# Telemetry sinks rotated by .claude/hooks/lib/log-rotation.sh — wildcard
# covers `.<sink>.jsonl`, `.<sink>-YYYY-MM.jsonl`, `.<sink>-YYYY-MM.jsonl.gz`,
# and any HHMMSSN-suffixed collision archive.
.claude/.rule-incidents*
.claude/.monitor-arms*
# Freeze edit-lock runtime state (.claude/hooks/lib/freeze-lock.sh) — a single
# worktree-local line holding the active allowed path prefix; never committed.
.claude/.freeze*
.claude/.skill-invocations*
.claude/.skill-edit-rejections*
.claude/.session-tokens*
# F2 prod-write defer-gate sinks (.claude/hooks/prod-write-defer-gate.sh):
# - approvals.jsonl: 1-year TTL, operator-email PII; gitignored-local-only.
# - denied.jsonl reserved for F1 (currently roadmap; see PERMISSION-DENIED-PAYLOAD-SHAPE.md).
.claude/logs/
# Stray Claude Code subagent worktree markers — must never be committed (#2905)
/.claude/worktrees/
.playwright-mcp/
.env
# The mktemp sibling a generated bootstrap.sh writes beside its .env (operator-bootstrap)
.env.tmp.*
# Generated bootstrap.sh run ledger — names-never-values local state written
# beside the script in a TRACKED spec dir; committing it conflicts with every
# branch that re-runs the bootstrap.
bootstrap-runs.jsonl
_site/
_site_test/
screenshot-gate-failures/

# Local state (since-id, caches -- do not commit)
.soleur/

knowledge-base/private/

# Generated knowledge-base caches (ADR-235). Each is a pure function of the tree, or -- for
# the rule-metrics aggregate -- of gitignored local incident data, so none of them is
# committed. They were, until #8377: a committed generated file conflicts with every other
# branch that touches the same tree, and GitHub's server-side merge cannot run the local merge
# driver that used to resolve one of them. Every main advance re-BEHINDs every open PR under
# strict required checks; the 71 of 102 first-parent main commits in one week that touched
# INDEX.md also made every open PR that touched it DIRTY -- the one state the admin hatch
# cannot cross.
#
# Regenerated on demand, never by a commit hook: scripts/ensure-kb-index.sh for the three
# index files (called by kb-search, learnings-researcher, the retrieval bench, `prepare` and
# SessionStart), and scripts/rule-prune.sh for the aggregate, which runs the aggregator ahead
# of its own read.
#
# NOT listed here, deliberately:
# knowledge-base/engineering/architecture/diagrams/model.likec4.json. That one is a PRODUCT --
# the web-platform C4 viewer (app/api/kb/c4/project/route.ts) fetches the committed blob from
# GitHub on the request path, with no build step -- so it has to exist as a committed blob. It
# stays committed and is regenerated on conflict by
# plugins/soleur/scripts/resolve-regenerable-conflicts.sh.
knowledge-base/INDEX.md
knowledge-base/kb-tags.txt
knowledge-base/kb-categories.txt
knowledge-base/project/rule-metrics.json
knowledge-base/.kb-index.stamp

# Screenshot and video artifacts (browser tests, feature demos, image generation)
*.png
tmp/

# Legitimate image assets (negate the blanket *.png rule)
!plugins/soleur/docs/images/*.png
!plugins/soleur/docs/images/blog/*.png
!plugins/soleur/docs/screenshots/*.png
!apps/web-platform/public/icons/*.png
!knowledge-base/product/design/**/screenshots/*.png
!knowledge-base/product/design/brand/**/*.png
!knowledge-base/engineering/operations/runbooks/screenshots/**/*.png
!knowledge-base/settings/team-icons/*.png
!knowledge-base/settings/team-icons/*.svg
!knowledge-base/settings/team-icons/*.webp
apps/web-platform/supabase/.temp/

# Per-tenant TF provisioning roots (generated by provision-* skills)
provisioning/

# Ephemeral capture scripts (sdk-probe)
apps/web-platform/scripts/capture-*
artifacts/

# Stage 0 spike throwaway workspace + raw-run artifacts
.spike-workspace/
knowledge-base/project/plans/spike-raw-*.json

# CI-vendored plugin tree (#3045) — populated by reusable-release.yml's
# "Vendor plugin into build context" step before docker build. Local devs
# building the image manually run the same `cp -r` command; never commit.
apps/web-platform/_plugin-vendored/

# Mutation testing report directories (#3121 / #3130). Allowlisted in
# .gitleaks.toml as a defense-in-depth in case a report ever lands by
# accident — but the primary control is this gitignore.
reports/mutation/
.stryker-tmp/
mutants/
/.AGENTS.md.source
# Defence-in-depth behind session-rules-loader.sh resolving its root with
# `git rev-parse --show-toplevel` (#8611): a loader older than that fix rooted on the
# session cwd and planted manifests under e.g. apps/web-platform/.claude/, where the
# untracked file made resolve-regenerable-conflicts.sh refuse. `**/` because an inner
# slash otherwise root-anchors the pattern. The sibling `.claude/.*` sinks above stay
# root-anchored on purpose: their writers root on BASH_SOURCE / CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR.
**/.claude/.session-manifests/

# Compound Promotion Loop (#2720). promotion-config.yml is TRACKED so the
# cron's actions/checkout can read it; default-OFF safety comes from the
# committed `enabled: false` line, not from the file's absence. Flipping
# to true requires a committed PR that operators can review.
# Defensive: the cron is stateless (week-cap derived from open
# self-healing/auto PRs, not from state files). Reject any future
# .github/promotion-*.json re-introduction.
.github/promotion-*.json

# #6695 — collector-status sidecar written into the cron spawn cwd; run-scoped,
# never committed (also structurally excluded in _cron-safe-commit.ts).
.soleur-collector-status/
.claude/.memory-backstop*

# ADR-191: npm is the single lockfile of record. bun remains the test runner, so a
# habitual `bun install` still recreates these -- scripts/lint-dual-lockfile.sh scans
# TRACKED files, so without this a stray lockfile is invisible until a commit resurrects
# the dual-lockfile split that made every Dependabot PR born red (#7084). Ignoring them
# makes resurrection structurally impossible rather than merely detectable after the fact.
bun.lock
bun.lockb

# post-dispatch-watch-gate state (per-worktree, never committed)
soleur-pending-dispatch
